## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

**Modified files:**
1. `package.json` - Added `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 as a dependency
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated to include the new dependency and its sub-dependencies
3. `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component to the root layout

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I:

1. **Installed the package**: Added `@vercel/analytics` using npm, which updated both package.json and package-lock.json

2. **Integrated Analytics**: 
   - Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next` at the top of the layout file
   - Added the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body section, following Next.js App Router best practices
   - Placed it after all other components to ensure proper tracking initialization

3. **Preserved existing structure**: The Analytics component was added without modifying any existing code, maintaining:
   - All existing imports and stylesheet declarations
   - The Shiny CSS loading order
   - The NuqsAdapter and AskProvider wrappers
   - Body class script injection for mobile-first responsive behavior

### Verification

✅ **Build**: Next.js build completed successfully with no errors
✅ **Linting**: No new linting errors introduced (existing warnings remain unchanged)
✅ **Tests**: All passing tests continue to pass (pre-existing test failures remain unaffected)
✅ **Type checking**: TypeScript compilation successful

### Next Steps

To enable analytics data collection:
1. Navigate to Analytics in your Vercel project dashboard
2. Click "Enable" to activate analytics for this project
3. Deploy the changes to production

Analytics will begin collecting data immediately upon deployment to Vercel.
